Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

All,

Attached are references documenting the failure of a 30" DR9 PE water trans=
mission line in Florida.  It failed in 10 years.  The suspected cause of fa=
ilure is oxidative degradation due to the presence of chlorine disinfectant=
s.

The first attachment has the project parameters.  Note that this is the sec=
ond such failure this Florida utility has experienced in a different bore c=
rossing.  It took 10 years for the failure to occur.

The second attachment shows a picture of the crack which was 13' long.  Thi=
s is a classic "brittle" failure due to the slow crack growth failure mode =
that ultimately ends the life of all PE pipe.  Note the lack of extreme def=
ormation that is present in a ductile failure due to the creep rupture fail=
ure mode.

The third attachment is email traffic in which the internal surface of the =
pipe is examined.  In this case there is evidence of oxidative degradation =
that is revealed by the "checkerboarding".  Their investigation will reveal=
 whether the oxidative degradation from chlorine disinfectants was the dire=
ct cause of the slow crack growth failure.  The picture at the bottom is a =
light magnification of the pipe ID.  As you can see the surface is rough.  =
The picture at the bottom is after a bend back test that reveals the "check=
erboarding" when these minute imperfections are amplified by the strain app=
lied.

The fourth attachment examines the fracture surface.  The pictures show the=
 classic surface of a slow crack growth failure.  The stress whitened fract=
ure surface would have been a very slow propagation zone of the crack.  The=
n you see the fracture surface is very dark.  This is the part of the crack=
 that propagated almost instantaneously.  What is counter intuitive is that=
 this failure mode occurs due to low "average" stresses...in time.   The li=
ttle circular features on the ID of the pipe in the fracture surface are po=
ints of initiation.  As you can see there are many of these.

Of course it is ironic that this mess is being repaired with a PVC solution=
.

When this sort of fracture surface is present in a fusion joint it is almos=
t always declared a "cold" weld and improper fusion.  The reality is it is =
a slow crack growth failure that occurs in a fusion joint because the fusio=
n joint has reduced capability compared to that of the pipe.  Recall Info B=
lurt 44.  The contractor gets thrown under the bus.

Regards,
John



