Below are additional pics of the 30=94 DIPS DR9 HDPE specimen from Florida.=
   The fracture surface have been exposed.  Pic on upper left shows both si=
des of the fracture surface with the inner pipe surfaces centered and facin=
g each other .  Upper right pic is an enlargement of the  lower half of the=
 specimen in pic 31.  2nd row of pics are microscopic enlargements of appar=
ent initiation points within the 12=94 long sample we received. It would ap=
pear that there are multiple initiations along the inner wall surface. Wall=
 thickness  is ~3.8=94.  The sample we received would appear to have at lea=
st 1 more initiation point to the left of the end of the specimens as orien=
ted.  Would speculate that since the fracture is in the 15=92 range in leng=
th that there may be more localized initiation points along the fracture.



Fracture surface would appear to have  classic slow crack growth features w=
ith evidence of multiple rings showing how crack propagated in this area. T=
he localized initiation points appear discolored to a brown tint.  Unknown =
as to what has caused this. In the upper right pic there appears to be an a=
rea along the inner surface that shows some edge cracking.  This may be ind=
ication of embrittlement in this area.



Bend back is in progress and inconclusive  at this point.  Specimen for ben=
d back needs to be cut smaller and thinner to allow bending by hand.  Will =
select a more specific location and cut to size in the area of the apparent=
 checker boarding.











